//? Title: Latent Visualization: What Two Coordinates Keep
//? Subtitle: Frozen autoencoder codes, fitting-only SVD projections and neighborhood diagnostics
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A two-dimensional picture retains only part of a learned representation. This report freezes
a 32-code MNIST autoencoder and fits PCA separately to its fitting codes and to fitting pixels.
Both projections use centered thin SVD with sample variances and frozen transforms. The code
picture retains 8.4% of pixel-space top-ten neighbors; the full 32-code representation retains
40.8%. Held-out one-neighbor label accuracy is 32.5% in the code picture and 78% in full codes,
compared with 89% in pixels and 88% in pixel PCA32. Pixel PCA32 also has lower reconstruction
MSE than this small autoencoder. A complete prerequisite exposes all 96 training updates;
projection and retrieval then make zero model updates. All images, neighbors and failures remain.
)
\toc

> A display is an additional projection

The frozen autoencoder maps 784 pixel coordinates to 32 ReLU code coordinates. Two display
coordinates are obtained by fitting PCA to those 32-dimensional fitting codes. Pixel PCA is a
separate linear baseline fitted directly to 784-dimensional fitting images. Both use only the
1,000 fitting observations to estimate their means and axes; validation and test observations
receive frozen transforms. Digit labels color held-out points and score fixed neighbor lists
after the projections are fitted.

PCA here uses the centered data matrix's thin SVD, following the centered, unscaled convention
of [R's prcomp](https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/prcomp.html).
Components are columns of V; sample variances are squared singular values divided by N-1.
Signs are arbitrary across implementations, and equal singular values permit subspace rotations.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/visualization_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(41, 1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle st;
  st.width     = 5.7;
  st.height    = 2.6;
  st.font_size = 18;
  d.node("x", {0, 5}, "Original pixel rows\n784 coordinates", st)
      .node("e", {8, 5}, "Frozen autoencoder\n32 ReLU codes", st)
      .node("p", {16, 5}, "Fitting-code PCA\n32 -> 2 display coordinates", st)
      .node("v", {24, 5}, "Held-out display\nLabels color fixed points", st)
      .edge("x", "e")
      .edge("e", "p")
      .edge("p", "v")
      .node("q", {8, -3}, "Fitting-pixel PCA\n784 -> 32 / first 2", st)
      .node("r", {16, -3}, "Inverse projection\nMeasure discarded information", st)
      .edge("x", "q")
      .edge("q", "r")
      .text(
          {12, -8},
          "Fitting rows determine means, axes and display limits.\nFive fixed geometries retrieve "
          "fitting neighbors; labels enter posthoc diagnostics.",
          20)
      .save_svg("build/visualization_method.svg");
}
```
