> Reconstruction loss and neighborhood retention quantify the display

For this checkpoint, the AE's held-out MSE is 0.050326. Inverse-projecting its two display
coordinates and decoding raises that error to 0.063673. Pixel PCA32 gives raw MSE 0.017631,
and clipping its reconstructed pixels to [0,1] reduces that to 0.015966. Pixel PCA2 gives raw
MSE 0.056757. These are different fitted models, numerical dtypes and losses; the shared count
of 32 coordinates does not match parameter count, optimization budget or serialized bit rate.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/visualization_reconstruction_errors.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz("build/visualization/analysis.npz"))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  const auto                     target = n::models::DoubleSampleRows(a.at("test_images"));
  const std::vector<std::string> fields{
      "test_ae_reconstruction",
      "ae_projected2_decoder_reconstruction",
      "pixel_pca_test_reconstruction",
      "pixel_pca_test_reconstruction",
      "pixel_pca2_test_reconstruction"},
      names{
          "AE32",
          "AE display2 -> decoder",
          "Pixel PCA32 raw",
          "Pixel PCA32 clipped",
          "Pixel PCA2 raw"};
  std::vector<double> x, error;
  for (int i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
    const auto raw = n::models::DoubleSampleRows(a.at(fields[i]));
    x.push_back(i);
    error.push_back(n::mean(n::square((i == 3 ? n::clip(raw, 0., 1.) : raw) - target)).item());
  }
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.bars(x, error, "Test pixel MSE", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, .65)
      .x_ticks(x, names)
      .x_label("Frozen representation / reconstruction rule")
      .y_label("Mean squared pixel error")
      .title("Reconstruction error includes the information discarded for display")
      .save_svg("build/visualization_reconstruction_errors.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/visualization_reconstruction_errors.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All errors use the same 200 held-out targets. Raw and clipped PCA32 results remain separate.)
\alttext(Five measured held-out reconstruction MSE bars for AE32, inverse-projected AE display2, raw and clipped pixel PCA32, and pixel PCA2.)

One-neighbor accuracy is 89% in pixels, 88% in pixel PCA32, 78% in AE32, 35% in pixel PCA2
and 32.5% in code PCA2. Top-ten overlap with pixel neighbors is 78.05% for pixel PCA32,
40.8% for AE32, 11% for pixel PCA2 and 8.4% for code PCA2. Color clusters therefore need to
be read alongside the losses and the neighbor geometry. The label probe is descriptive and
has no repeated-seed or uncertainty analysis.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/visualization_neighbor_diagnostics.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz("build/visualization/analysis.npz"))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  const std::vector<std::string> spaces{"pixel", "pca32", "ae32", "pca2", "ae2"},
      names{"Pixels", "Pixel PCA32", "AE32", "Pixel PCA2", "Code PCA2"};
  std::vector<double> x, accuracy, overlap;
  for (int i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
    x.push_back(i);
    const auto list = a.at(spaces[i] + "_neighbors");
    accuracy.push_back(
        n::models::NeighborLabelAccuracy(list, a.at("fit_labels"), a.at("test_labels")));
    overlap.push_back(n::models::NeighborOverlap(a.at("pixel_neighbors"), list));
  }
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.points(x, accuracy, "1NN accuracy", {37, 99, 235}, 4.)
      .points(x, overlap, "Pixel top10 overlap", {220, 38, 38}, 4.)
      .x_ticks(x, names)
      .y_limits(0, 1.05)
      .x_label("Geometry of fixed fitting-neighbor search")
      .y_label("Descriptive fraction")
      .title("Two display coordinates lose many original pixel neighbors")
      .save_svg("build/visualization_neighbor_diagnostics.svg");
}
```
